04e1c9a-2b0a-483d-af91-49e774ebd61e","position":{"commit_sha":"efd81e11640d966264c58dca119e1a38beeef9f7","position":"1786657293422984001-804e1c9a-2b0a-483d-af91-49e774ebd61e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"da9bcff1e1ea7e2289bc7acbce3e44d96f30f07b34688a63e19ba03fc06b15e7","event_uuid":"52357dc7-4e81-456d-913a-cd427bc3e2b0","position":{"commit_sha":"1c837af132cac3da4c49237f4594022b4004f7e1","position":"1786657571227858001-52357dc7-4e81-456d-913a-cd427bc3e2b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786160042328371001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0eb457ee-0808-42be-a3a5-d27c19c439ef","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"544a-2f6f-6ed7-4409"},{"link_uuid":"f60d355f-da20-40cb-b975-512625719471","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c38c-fe02-5039-4c79"},{"link_uuid":"cfb4aeda-ef22-49b8-aafb-d42c4f10e302","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bd54-5098-f623-449f"},{"link_uuid":"571fb022-a337-473c-8f70-a8c07eb713ee","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"18c0-777e-4d5e-4429"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe bridge has nowhere to record which tracker projects a store syncs, nor which repos each\nproject's tickets belong to. Epic `0e68-41eb-5782-4336` needs that mapping to be a property of the\n**store**, not of any one repo: `.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json` is shared by every repo using the\nstore, so if two repos fetched different project subsets against one shared snapshot, each pass would\ndiff the other's projects as remote deletions.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `.bridge_state/projects.json` beside the committed bridge state (`bindings.json`,\n`prev_snapshot.json`), owned by a new `projects_store.py` module rather than by extending\n`binding_store.py` (different write cadences; an operator editing the mapping must not rewrite the\nlarge bindings record).\n\nRecord shape:\n\n```json\n{\"version\": 1, \"legacy_default\": \"REB\", \"projects\": {\"REB\": {\"repos\": [\"rebar\"]}}}\n```\n\nThe `projects` key set **is** the store's sync list (no second list to keep in agreement).\n`legacy_default` is the project that pre-epic tickets resolve to. Per ADR 0060 the mapping changes\nonly on an operator edit, so it adds no per-pass tickets-branch growth.\n\nSurface it as `bridge projects` under the verb group (`src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`), with\nlibrary and MCP parity (epic `2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3`). The bridge library surface is\n`src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`. The MCP layer splits by mutation: `list` is a read tool (`_mcp_reads.py`,\n`register_read_tools`, READ_ONLY), `set`/`remove` are write tools (`_mcp_writes.py`,\n`register_write_tools`); `mcp_server.py` registers both. Sub-verbs: `list`, `set <KEY> --repos a,b`,\n`remove <KEY>`. `set` on an existing key **replaces** its repos list (idempotent; drop a repo by\nre-issuing `set` without it).\n\nThe bridge group help is a pinned byte-exact contract: the listing in\n`src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt` served by `_help.subcommand_help`, plus the parser's hardcoded\n`metavar` verb set. Adding a verb means editing both the help file and the metavar.\n\nThe module exposes two functions so I/O and rule are separable: `load_mapping(repo_root)` reads and\nvalidates the record; `resolve_project(ticket, mapping) -> str | None` is a pure function over a\nloaded mapping (tri-state rule unit-testable without a store on disk).\n\nRead behaviour when the record is missing or bad follows `compat.py`'s precedent for\n`.store-compat.json`: an **absent** record is legal and reads as an empty mapping with a\n`legacy_default` of `None`; a **malformed** one raises rather than degrading to a permissive default.\nAbsent is legal because an ensure unit seeds the record at init / `fsck --repair` / MCP boot; until\nthen every ticket resolves to `None` and nothing syncs (fail-safe). That ensure-seed unit is NOT built here: it is delivered by the dependent sibling story 462d-8d84 (legacy-store migration), which seeds `.bridge_state/projects.json` via ensure units in `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py` and `ensures.py`. This story delivers only the store module, its helpers, `resolve_project`, and the CLI/library/MCP surface; the seed lands in 462d within this same epic, so the fail-safe `None` state is transitional, not permanent.\n\n`resolve_project` implements the tri-state rule so inbound and outbound stories consume one\nimplementation:\n\n| ticket `bridge_project` | returns | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| key absent from state | the mapping's `legacy_default` (str) | legacy ticket |\n| `\"\"` (explicit empty) | `None` | deliberately not synced |\n| `\"REB\"` | `\"REB\"` | sync into that project |\n\n`None` is the not-synced sentinel: callers treat `None` as \"emit no mutation\" and any non-`None`\nresult as a project key safe to target. A `legacy_default` that is itself empty also yields `None`,\nso an unconfigured store degrades to \"nothing syncs\".\n\n`--repos` is **required** on `set` (omitting it is an argument error, non-zero exit). `--repos \"\"` is\nthe explicit way to store an empty list, keeping \"no default repo\" deliberate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py` — the subcommand and the hardcoded `metavar` verb set\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt` — the pinned group help listing\n- `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` — the `list` read tool\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` — the `set` and `remove` write tools\n- tests under `tests/`\n\nThe parent epic's file impact names `projects_store.py` (not `binding_store.py`). `_mcp_writes.py`\nis shared with the sibling adding ticket create arguments; that sibling `depends_on` this story, so\nthe two are strictly ordered and never edited concurrently.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard's CLI row — a real CLI subprocess with a persisted-state assertion (the\nmechanism spans argument parsing, the on-disk JSON record, and exit codes).\n\n- Happy path: `bridge projects set REB --repos rebar` in a fresh store, then `list` returns the\n  entry and `.bridge_state/projects.json` contains it.\n- Cross-surface: an entry written through the library is read back byte-equal through the CLI and\n  through MCP (one record, not three).\n- Failure: `bridge projects remove NOPE` on a store without that key exits non-zero, names the key,\n  leaves the record byte-unchanged.\n- Edge: `set REB --repos` with an empty list stores `[]`.\n- Replace-not-merge: `set REB --repos a,b` then `set REB --repos a` stores exactly `[\"a\"]`.\n- Pinned help: `rebar bridge` and `rebar help bridge` render text naming `projects`, and the\n  argparse `metavar` matches the pinned listing.\n- Collateral invariant: after any mapping write, `bindings.json` and `prev_snapshot.json` hash\n  identically to before.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `bridge projects set|list|remove` exist under the bridge verb group and operate on\n      `.bridge_state/projects.json`; a CLI subprocess test asserts the on-disk record after each verb.\n- [x] The library and MCP surfaces read and write the same record as the CLI; a test writes through\n      one surface and reads the identical entry through the other two.\n- [x] `resolve_project` returns `legacy_default` for an absent field, `None` for explicit empty, the\n      key for a set value, and `None` when `legacy_default` is itself empty; a parameterized unit\n      test asserts the exact return value for all four cases.\n- [x] `set` without `--repos` is an argument error exiting non-zero; a paired CLI subprocess test.\n- [x] `set --repos \"\"` stores `[]`; asserted in the same paired CLI subprocess test.\n- [x] An absent record reads as an empty mapping with a `None` legacy default while a malformed one\n      raises; a paired test over a store with no record and one with truncated JSON.\n- [x] `list` carries the READ_ONLY annotation and `set`/`remove` are registered by\n      `register_write_tools`; asserted by inspecting the registered tools.\n- [x] A mapping write leaves `bindings.json` and `prev_snapshot.json` byte-identical; hashed before\n      and after in the CLI test.\n- [x] `remove` of an unknown key exits non-zero and mutates nothing.\n- [x] `set` on an already-present key replaces its repos list rather than merging; the stored list\n      equals exactly the second call's argument.\n- [x] The pinned group help in `bridge.txt` and the parser `metavar` both name `projects`; a test\n      asserts the rendered `rebar bridge` help contains the verb and that the pinned file and the\n      `metavar` verb set agree.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"projects mapping store + tri-state resolve_project"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"bridge projects set/list/remove CLI verbs"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt","reason":"pinned bridge group help naming projects verb"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"library facade for projects mapping read/write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"MCP bridge_projects_list read tool"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"MCP bridge_projects_set/remove write tools"},{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"export projects mapping facade from library surface"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated CLI reference for new bridge projects verbs"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"regenerated MCP reference for new bridge_projects tools"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","reason":"classify new bridge_projects MCP tools in coverage partition"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_happy.py","reason":"CLI happy-path oracle for bridge projects verbs"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_heldout.py","reason":"CLI held-out oracle for bridge projects verbs"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py","reason":"projects store happy-path oracle"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py","reason":"projects store held-out oracle"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bridge_projects_surfaces_heldout.py","reason":"cross-surface parity held-out oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","18c0-777e-4d5e-4429"],["relates_to","544a-2f6f-6ed7-4409"],["relates_to","bd54-5098-f623-449f"],["relates_to","c38c-fe02-5039-4c79"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"b36e34d2-0324-4d8a-8ca5-97585062867d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c927-0a68-4465-42a2","ticket_type":"story","title":"bridge projects: store-level project-to-repos mapping and its CLI, library and MCP surface","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["14daaaff-d4fa-4109-8817-1df3f6d6b2d1","231a3132-90a7-47f7-9a7a-2d9508266680","b5cbfb07-9b67-4b27-ad65-0f0f2f2bf41e","81151efe-0a8e-4697-a132-1052ac85bd86","130d46c1-0ad7-4668-b51d-3f4abed49faa","5712cdb9-7b1f-464a-863e-2cc6f90894a3","c4791426-8ba7-4094-919a-9eab5c827573","ba14822a-a571-472c-bd1e-728ada15f8e8","03e025fc-1f72-41fd-9a52-0c7b6edb285e","35b9b6d8-fd7b-4312-bb03-917b518bf0ea","b36e34d2-0324-4d8a-8ca5-97585062867d","d1b6129d-870f-4426-b3b7-892cac5b6d61","0eb457ee-0808-42be-a3a5-d27c19c439ef","f60d355f-da20-40cb-b975-512625719471","cfb4aeda-ef22-49b8-aafb-d42c4f10e302","571fb022-a337-473c-8f70-a8c07eb713ee","81f3cf15-2ce5-4b8c-9a01-00b81d0e4269","1f078f80-6417-4292-9195-9aa4203f874c","804e1c9a-2b0a-483d-af91-49e774ebd61e","52357dc7-4e81-456d-913a-cd427bc3e2b0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786657571227858002,"uuid":"ee9a23bc-ae03-4135-93d1-fc4e8026ea05"}